course: dictionary
lesson: 1111
title: Bravo
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Bravo!» is a shout that means well done. People shout it to praise someone who has done something very well, often at the end of a show. Here it works as an exclamation, a word that gives a burst of feeling on its own.
explain: «The driver laughs, but the gentleman says, "Bravo, ma'am!"» The gentleman is pleased with her, so he is praising her. Ask who is speaking and how they feel. The clues tell you that bravo means well done.
explain: Bravo has two other meanings. It is also the code word for the letter B when spelling aloud: Alpha, Bravo, Charlie. In old stories, a bravo was a hired thug or killer, but that is an old meaning, so you will rarely meet it today.
fact: «Bravo» is shouted to praise someone who has done something very well.
fact: At a show, the audience shouts «Bravo!» and claps.
fact: «Bravo» is the code word for the letter B when spelling letters aloud.
fact: «Bravo» comes from Italian.
fact: In old stories, a bravo was a hired thug or killer.
exercise: The crowd claps after the singer's last note and shouts «Bravo!» What does bravo mean here? | *Well done | Go away | Goodbye | Be quiet
exercise: The army radio says «B for Bravo» when spelling a name. Which letter does Bravo stand for? | *The letter B | The letter C | The letter D | The letter A
exercise: In old stories, a «bravo» was a hired thug. What was a bravo in those stories? | A kind teacher | *A hired thug or killer | A French cook | A kind of dance
test: The teacher writes «Bravo!» on your page. What is she doing? | Scolding you for being late | Counting your marks | *Praising your good work | Asking a question
test: Where does the word bravo come from? | German | *Italian | Swahili | Arabic
exam: In «If you can solve these, you have travelled the whole course … bravo, et à bientôt!», what does bravo show? | Tiredness | Anger | Sadness | *Praise, well done
